  "notes": "{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ means to overcome or triumph over something. It has a strong, dramatic tone and is often used for significant challenges or adversities.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜に{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to overcome ~, to triumph over ~\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {困難|こんなん}に{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to overcome difficulties\n- {誘惑|ゆうわく}に{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to resist temptation\n- {逆境|ぎゃっきょう}に{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to triumph over adversity\n- {病気|びょうき}に{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to conquer an illness\n- {恐怖|きょうふ}に{打|う}ち{勝|か}つ: to overcome fear\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {克服|こくふく}する: to overcome (more formal, often for abstract challenges)\n- {勝|か}つ: to win (more general)\n- {乗|の}り{越|こ}える: to get over, to surmount",
